Friend Class in C++

 *Description* 

This C++ program demonstrates the use of a friend class. The "Auditor" class is declared as a friend of the "Account" class, allowing it to access the private "balance" member directly.

 *Concepts Used* 

- Classes and Objects
- Encapsulation
- Private Data Members
- Friend Class
- Constructors

 *Working* 

- "Account" contains a private variable "balance".
- "Auditor" is declared as a friend class using "friend class Auditor;".
- Because of this, "Auditor" can access the private "balance" of "Account".
- The "inspect()" function displays the account balance.
- An account with an initial balance of "5000.0" is created.

 *Sample Output* 

Account Balance: 5000

 *Objective* 

To understand how a friend class can access the private members of another class while maintaining controlled access.
